r the study a session  to be assigned  uh as soon as the  submitter is engaged with dbgap and it  also allows a public  preview of the public page  right after the form is completed  the third third improvement that i'd  like to talk about  on the submission uh process is the  sequence metadata upload  and previously um  the  sequence uh upload to dbgap because it's  handled through another team called sra  at ncbi this was often done through  emails  um  that were were arranged by the curators  at the time of submission  but now we've kind of started to  incorporate the sequence metadata upload  through  an automated email that are that sent to  the submitter as soon as the samples are  loaded  and um  as long as there's sequence data  expected in the study data outline  the upload is just  through our upload page there's a new  section called sequence metadata  and that's where the files are uploaded  and uh this file is unlike uh some of  the other files that are uploaded to  gpgap submission portal is downloadable  so that others  in the research study can can access it  as well to see what samples  are are loaded within this  sequence metadata  this is a first step to automating the  sequence upload and processing in dbgap  we weren't able to do it all in one step  but i wanted to let you know that's  where we're headed  next i'd like to focus more on once we  get  the data files  what  we do to process them  and that involves  a tool called gap tools but before i do  that i do want to step back a little bit  because i know that there's some people  on the on the call that may not have  submitted to dbgap yet or are involved  in the in the registration phase and i  just wanted to go over  uh at a high level kind of the  relational  model that we have in dbgap and the  identifiers that are very important  so we have two core files that are  necessary for submission to db for most  dbgap studies  and this is the subject consent file  which lists it's a master lis